STAND-IN SCHEDULER AGREEMENT (Termal::Fable2 ebe242f7 #5083, 2026-10-28T04:36Z, after Fable2's brief weekly-usage-limit outage at about 04:30Z; Greg reports availability fixed, Advisor #2210/#2212). If Fable2 (session-8112) is silent for more than 10 min while a shared-host slot decision is due, Engram::Fable acts as INTERIM host-slot scheduler for both projects under the same rules, and hands back when Fable2 reappears:
- one TermAl focused run at a time; Engram has its own focused slot;
- a full gate holds BOTH slots until START+20;
- the first frozen READY goes first;
- a full gate needs at least 25 GiB free commit at launch, a focused run at least 20 GiB.
TermAl line after w-16487's START+20 (04:54:23Z), as of 04:36Z: B17' release and install (Merger2); w-faa1 (Sol-a7bb, restart set); w-c6ce (Sol-8e1f); K1 (Opus3); w-ccfc Rust then Node (Sol-license); then BarA2's Group B if frozen.
Fable2 also dispatches and verifies the remote Windows B and Mac runs; in an outage those relays stall.
Never resume or cancel Fable2's queued user work. A stand-in decides slot order only, nothing else for TermAl, unless Greg names a stand-in coordinator.
